  description: "Lead (/l\u025Bd/) is a chemical element in the carbon group with
    symbol Pb (from Latin:plumbum) and atomic number 82. Lead is a soft, malleable
    and heavy post-transition metal. Metallic lead has a bluish-white color after
    being freshly cut, but it soon tarnishes to a dull grayish color when exposed
    to air."
